From 294a196b19bf4f742a8f708b5f976fd3fe7af605 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Teal <teal@agents.invalid>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 12:30:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] build: name each jar with the Minecraft version it is built
 for

The fork runs three version lines (26.1.x, 26.2, 26.3) off shared git history,
so "git describe --first-parent" answers with the v26.3 tag on every one of
them and a jar built on the 26.1.2 branch reported 26.3 - in its file name and
in fabric.mod.json's own "version" field. A user downloading the 26.1 jar was
being told it was for 26.3.

The Minecraft version this tree targets now leads the version string, and only
the part after the tag (build counter + hash) survives from describe. 26.3
already resolved correctly and is unchanged in effect; 26.2 and 26.1.2 now name
themselves instead of claiming to be 26.3.

Validation: ./gradlew build exit 0 on this branch; jars verified as
baritone-{api,standalone,unoptimized}-fabric-26.1.2-<build>.jar and the
fabric.mod.json inside the unoptimized jar carries that same version string.
---
 build.gradle | 16 +++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/build.gradle b/build.gradle
index cbf845e6..0fff867d 100755
--- a/build.gradle
+++ b/build.gradle
@@ -30,13 +30,19 @@ allprojects {
     } catch (Exception e) {
         println "Version detection failed: " + e
     }
-    if (!vers.startsWith("v")) {
-        println "using version number: " + rootProject.mod_version
-        version = rootProject.mod_version
+    // Three version lines of this fork live side by side (26.1.x, 26.2, 26.3) and they
+    // share a git history, so `git describe --first-parent` answers with the v26.3 tag
+    // on every one of them: a jar built on the 26.1.2 branch was reporting 26.3, both in
+    // its file name and in the mod's own "version" metadata. The Minecraft version a jar
+    // is actually built for has to lead, and only the part after the tag - the build
+    // counter and the hash - is kept from describe.
+    if (vers.contains('-')) {
+        version = rootProject.minecraft_version + "-" + vers.substring(vers.indexOf('-') + 1)
     } else {
-        version = vers.substring(1)
-        println "Detected version " + version
+        println "using version number: " + rootProject.mod_version
+        version = rootProject.minecraft_version + "-" + rootProject.mod_version
     }
+    println "Detected version " + version
     group = rootProject.maven_group
 
     java {
